Z||000000||SCFIERO||12-12-2000||05:53 PM||||How can one tell what tranny they have?  I have an 86 GT 5spd, and an 87 GT auto.  Any help would be great.  Thanks<P><BR>Brian||||reg||5
Z||000001||Hank is Here||12-12-2000||06:01 PM||||The tranny in the 86 GT if stock should be the Getrag.  All Fiero auto trannies were the TH125, they did however have different final drive ratios.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||12-12-2000||06:06 PM||||Hank is right......if your '86 GT is stock, it will have a Getrag tranny.  The '87-'88 V-6 auto. trannies have 3.33 final drives......the "best" you could get in a Fiero (as far as acceleration is concerned). <P>'85-'86 V-6 autos have 3.06 final drives (I believe) and the 4 bangers were even higher (2.93??). ||||reg||1
Z||000003||SCFIERO||12-12-2000||06:09 PM||||Yes it is stock.  I will be disassembling from the engine it tonight.  How will I know if it needs to be rebuilt? Never drove the car so I don't know how it was driven.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Hank is Here||12-12-2000||06:13 PM||||That last one seems a little open ended.  Why was your car not running?  How long was it sitting?  I would say shoot for the known problem that had the car taken off the road, I doubt two things went wrong at the same time.   Only problems could then  be from sitting.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||SCFIERO||12-12-2000||06:16 PM||||The guy I bought it from ($400) said it had a blown head gasket.  The interior and exterior was in shambles.  Looks like he painted it with a spray can.  So I decided to refurbish the entire car.  Should I expect problems w/ the tranny?  What are the tale tale signs?||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||12-12-2000||07:11 PM||||The RPO sticker includes the tranny codes on it. The ones for the automatics are in my cave.||||reg||1
